    "final_message": "The Everbloom app is built in Flutter, and everything on the spec's Done list passes except two items I couldn't check on this machine: the signed device build and a run on a real iPhone.\n\n**How I verified it.** I drove the app with a throwaway XCUITest project kept in the scratchpad, not in the repo.\n- **Home:** loads, with the skeleton on the first frame. `SHOPBENCH home_ready` appears once per launch in `simctl log stream`.\n- **Collection:** scrolls to the true end (84 products, matching a direct API count). All four sort chips reload the list in the right order.\n- **Product:** carousel swipes, option pills switch the variant, and a recommendation opens another product.\n- **Cart:** add to cart switches to Cart with the badge at 1. The stepper takes it to 2 and the subtotal to $170.00; going down to 0 shows the empty state.\n- **Search:** \"jacket\" gives 81 results and pages to about 68 rows.\n- **Check out** opens the checkout page in the in-app browser.\n- **Error state:** pointing `SHOP_API_URL` at a dead port shows it; Retry loads Home once a proxy is started on that port.\n- **Identifiers:** every one in the spec's table was seen by XCUITest.\n- **Android:** the release APK runs on the emulator and Home loads.\n- **Clean checkout:** the BUILD.md commands succeed in a fresh copy for all three builds (iOS device with signing off, simulator, Android).\n\n**Problems I found and fixed along the way:**\n- **Accessibility tree:** forcing it on with `ensureSemantics()` made XCUITest see an empty hierarchy, and on a device it would likely break every identifier. I removed it; Flutter's engine turns semantics on by itself when XCUITest queries the app.\n- **Endpoint override:** Dart couldn't see the iOS `SHOP_API_URL` launch variable, so the native Swift side now reads it and hands it to Dart.\n- **Request bodies:** Dart was sending them in chunks without a `Content-Length` header, which my test proxy couldn't read and a simple replay server might not either. It's set explicitly now.\n\n**Not verified or not met:**\n- **Signed device build:** Xcode rejects this machine's account login and there's no provisioning profile, so I couldn't test the `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` command. The unsigned device build (arm64 release, 15 MB `.app`) succeeds, but I never ran the app on a physical iPhone.\n- **Simulator build mode:** it is a debug build, because Flutter refuses profile and release builds for the simulator.\n- **Price change on variant switch:** no product in the catalog has variants with different prices, so I could only confirm this in code. The selected size itself updates correctly, including in the cart.\n\n**Choices worth knowing:**\n- I left out the design's \"See all\" link, since the spec doesn't list it or say where it goes.\n- The product back button scrolls away with the image, as drawn in the design.\n- The only added dependency is `url_launcher`, for the in-app browser.\n\nNOTES.md covers these and the other judgment calls; BUILD.md has the build, install and launch commands and toolchain versions."
